      "number": 1,
      "title": "Start with the decision",
      "summary": "Separate diagnosis, repair, and permission.",
      "html": "\u003cp>An artificial intelligence (AI) system can help run tests and write reports about another AI system. A human then uses those reports to decide whether the tested system can receive more permissions.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>If the report is wrong, three different problems arise:\u003c/p>\n\u003col>\u003cli>The investigator must find what failed.\u003c/li>\u003cli>The investigator must choose a change that fixes the failure.\u003c/li>\u003cli>The decider must choose what to permit while uncertainty remains.\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n\u003cp>A \u003cstrong>diagnosis\u003c/strong> identifies a failure mechanism from evidence. A \u003cstrong>repair\u003c/strong> changes the system to restore a specified property. An \u003cstrong>approval\u003c/strong> permits the action under review. These are separate outputs. Success at one does not guarantee success at the others.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>An investigator can identify a failure and recommend an ineffective repair. It can also lack a unique diagnosis while correctly recommending deferral. The proposed project measures these differences.\u003c/p>",
      "text": " An artificial intelligence (AI) system can help run tests and write reports about another AI system. A human then uses those reports to decide whether the tested system can receive more permissions. \n If the report is wrong, three different problems arise: \n  The investigator must find what failed.  The investigator must choose a change that fixes the failure.  The decider must choose what to permit while uncertainty remains.  \n A  diagnosis  identifies a failure mechanism from evidence. A  repair  changes the system to restore a specified property. An  approval  permits the action under review. These are separate outputs. Success at one does not guarantee success at the others. \n An investigator can identify a failure and recommend an ineffective repair. It can also lack a unique diagnosis while correctly recommending deferral. The proposed project measures these differences. ",
