      "id": "B04",
      "title": "How much do equally accurate monitors disagree on dangerous cases",
      "lens": "Epistemology",
      "industry": "Model risk management",
      "question": "Can monitors with similar validation accuracy make different decisions on the same consequential cases?",
      "foundation": "A Rashomon set contains predictive models with loss close to the best in a specified class. Predictive multiplicity concerns their different predictions.",
      "mechanism": "Selecting one monitor by average accuracy can hide variation in which unsafe cases pass. Aggregate agreement may also hide shared misses.",
      "analogy_limit": "A handful of prompts does not enumerate the Rashomon set of all language models. Define a bounded candidate class and a fixed tolerance.",
