      "title": "Does independent evidence help more than an additional reviewer",
      "lens": "Reliability",
      "industry": "Power-system reliability",
      "question": "At equal review cost, does a fresh measurement prevent more shared misses than another model opinion?",
      "foundation": "Evidence independence differs from the number of agents. A common-cause failure can defeat several review stages at once.",
